Subject: Cantor Compact Coordination Session P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 5131426a-dbdf-43ee-8bb2-d4860aa4b57a
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Compact_Coordination_Session_P0.sop

& [Need] is a real hashed reentry control surface
  + the stateless tool proves semantics but repeats both context and growing checkpoint values
  + measurement rejects context-only optimization and shows recursive tool metadata is itself large
  + retaining context plus checkpoint makes ordinary control depend only on a compact exact handle

& [Safety] makes custody visible
  + registry record and handle are separately digest-bound
  + every mutation compare-and-sets registry session sequence and record
  + READ returns exact retained typed-state JSON and restart loss is explicit

& [ScopeChoice] is volatile before durable
  + process-local state permits concurrency and compactness proof without disk crash recovery key management or migration
  + persistence and authentication can later build on a proven exact state machine

& [Conclusion] is implement one volatile compact session tool beside rather than inside the stateless tool

